#. column 15: Just like water, the moments which make up life rush past in the blink of an eye. In recognition of this truth, the Hhetsarro have given the river which runs through Shaaloani the name “Niikwerepi”─the swift current of time. The two lakes into which it flows are in turn named after the morning and the evening, with Lake Toari alluding to the former.
